The same lines, and the ones that hold for every article type of the journal (title pages, anonymisation, statements, file type), stand as comments at the top of `main.tex`. Their sources, each with its address and date, are in `journals/requirements.json`.

## Files

| File | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `main.tex` | the manuscript: abbreviated title page (anonymized), abstract, body, references, figure legends |
| `title_page.tex` | the full title page (authors, institutions, funding, disclosures, data sharing statement): a separate file, not anonymized |
| `rsnastyle.tex`, `rsnafont.tex`, `rsnastyle.css` | the style: an 11-point Times font, double spacing, no page numbers, figures and tables at the end |
| `nejm.bbx`, `nejm.cbx` | the reference style |
| `sample_bibliography.bib` | sample references: replace them with yours |
| `latexmkrc` | the build settings |
| `manuscript.json` | what this repository was configured as |
| `scripts/`, `templates/`, `journals/`, `tests/` | the template's own machinery: what writes the skeleton, and the facts it is written from. They can stay. Once the journal and the article type are settled you may delete them; the build on GitHub goes on working |

## Build

On GitHub: every push builds `main.pdf` and `title_page.pdf`. Open Actions, the latest run of "Build", and download the PDFs under Artifacts. The build uses one fixed TeX Live, the image named by `TEXLIVE_IMAGE` at the top of `.github/workflows/build.yml`: it does not change until you change that line.

For a journal that takes the text as a Word file, the same run keeps an HTML copy of the manuscript: download the artifact `word-manuscript`, unpack it, open `main.html` in Microsoft Word and save it as a Word document. The copy is made by lwarp. It carries the text, the tables, the references and the list of abbreviations; how Word shows it has not been checked by the template, so read it through before you upload it.

On a laptop with TeX Live or MiKTeX (LuaLaTeX, latexmk, biber):

    latexmk

builds both PDFs. The HTML copy takes several more runs of LuaLaTeX, so it is made only when you ask for it:

    RSNA_HTML=1 latexmk             (Linux, macOS)
    $env:RSNA_HTML=1; latexmk       (Windows PowerShell; it stays set until you close the window)

makes `main.html` after the PDFs (lwarp needs the poppler tools `pdftotext` and `pdftocairo` for it). The template checks both commands on Linux; the HTML copy has not been tried on Windows or macOS, and the copy that GitHub keeps is the same one.

The font is Times New Roman where it is installed, and TeX Gyre Termes, a free font of the same shape that every TeX Live has, where it is not.

In Overleaf: New Project, Import from GitHub, this repository (or download it as a ZIP and use Upload Project). In Overleaf's menu, set the compiler to LuaLaTeX (the manuscript does not compile with pdfLaTeX) and the main document to `main.tex`. To print the full title page, set the main document to `title_page.tex` and compile once. A compile in Overleaf builds the PDF alone; to have Overleaf make the HTML copy as well, change `our $rsna_html = 0;` to `our $rsna_html = 1;` in `latexmkrc`, and change it back once you have the copy, because every compile then takes several more runs of LuaLaTeX and may reach the time limit of your Overleaf plan. The template has not been tried in Overleaf.

## Another journal or article type

    python scripts/configure.py --list
    python scripts/configure.py --journal "<<journal>>" --type "<<article_type>>" --title "..." --description "..."

(`python` on Windows, `python3` on macOS and Linux), or the form: Issues, New issue, "Configure the manuscript"; or Actions, "Configure manuscript", Run workflow. A file you have edited since the last configuration is never written over: the run stops and names it, unless you add `--force` on a laptop.

## Credit

Made from a community LaTeX template for manuscripts sent to the journals of the Radiological Society of North America (RSNA). It is not made or endorsed by the RSNA. The template descends from [cai4cai/RSNATemplate](https://github.com/cai4cai/RSNATemplate), whose style files, reference style and writing notes it keeps.
